p.src:
In the vacuum-dominated limit, $H=\sqrt{\frac{8\pi G}{3}\rho_0}.$ Then Hubble’s law becomes $v=Hd.$ The horizon is defined by $v=1$, so its distance is $d_H=\frac{1}{H}
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{8\pi G\rho_0/3}}.$ The rough number given here is about $10$ to $12$ billion light years.

